WEBVTT

NOTE English captions for https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fBzrLN77gng, from YouTube, repeats removed.

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:06.220
Then Imam al-Ghazali shares with us various narrations and stories of the pious predecessors.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.440
Wa Dhul-Qarnain who met an angel

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:15.640
Dhul-Qarnain whose story is mentioned in Surat al-Kahf

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:19.620
he once met one of the angels and he said teach me something

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.980
that will increase my faith and certitude.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.800
And the angel said to him, "Do not become angry

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:27.240
because

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:29.920
the shaytan

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:31.120
has

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:32.979
a greater capability

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.620
of controlling the human being when he becomes angered.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:39.280
So,

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:40.360
respond

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:41.600
to anger

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.040
with by suppressing it.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:46.040
And

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:48.760
calm the fire of anger

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:49.980
with

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:50.940
uh

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:54.040
a ta'wuda which is uh being

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:57.000
the opposite of rushing and being

00:00:57.400 --> 00:00:59.140
rushed which is deliberation.

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:03.820
And calm the fire of anger with deliberation.

00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:06.840
You know, a lot of times especially when you're young

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:11.240
and especially in today's world there's so much going on and with social media you have

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:12.780
to have an opinion about everything.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:17.380
Everybody is a a commentator and an expert on everything that happens in the world.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:22.420
And then particularly people will want to know, you know, "What what what do

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:24.660
What does Islam have to say about this?"

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:31.400
Often times when things are going on in the world there's current events and

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:35.680
things that are taking place that are very hot topics.

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:38.480
The best response is to slow down.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:41.280
To really think about it.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:43.120
Everyone wants to be smart.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:47.340
Oh, I've got it figured out and I can be the the religious and social commentator

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:48.040
on this.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:49.320
But

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:51.780
you might say things that you'll regret later.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.240
A lot of times just let me think about it.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:57.000
A man once asked Imam al-Shafi'i Allah

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.540
a question and Imam Shafi'i was quiet.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:01.740
The man asked again.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.320
And Imam al-Shafi'i said, "Hold on.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:06.280
I'm still thinking about

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:11.700
whether answering your question or remaining quiet is more beloved to Allah.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:14.660
I'm still working on that piece.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:19.000
You know, a man a man came to Imam Malik and asked him all of these

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.360
questions. I don't know.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:21.400
I don't know.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:22.040
I don't know.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:23.400
And then he answered a few questions.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.240
He said, "Man, you don't know?

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:26.600
You're Imam Malik.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:28.140
Everybody says you know everything."

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:31.020
Imam Malik said, "Go out and tell people I don't know anything.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:33.380
It's okay. I'm not here to

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:35.060
entertain you.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:36.340
This is

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:38.360
This is knowledge of revelation.

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:39.320
I can't make it up.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:41.640
If I don't know, I have to say I don't know.

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:43.320
I have to think about it.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:44.300
I have to research.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:47.300
We have to contemplate, consult.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:49.980
All of these things are so important.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:52.020
And mashallah it's really

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:55.680
very encouraging to see so many young people in the room.

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:56.640
This is a skill

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:59.520
the sooner you you learn it the better.

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:01.560
Consult people.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:03.960
Think deeply about things.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:07.020
Often times your passion is a strength

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:14.760
but allow that passion and that strength to be guided by deliberation and and seeking advice

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:18.140
from people more experienced and wiser than yourself.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:20.980
Don't be someone who's reactionary.

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:25.060
There's a difference between taking initiative and being reactionary.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:29.660
Anger is a very reactionary response.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:32.780
So, here the angel is telling Dhul-Qarnain

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.580
calm your anger with deliberation.

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:39.900
Wa iyyaka wal 'ajalah and beware

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:41.660
of haste.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:43.660
Rushing.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:44.980
Got to

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:46.100
do it now.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:47.460
Jazakallahu khairan.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.560
Fa innaka idha 'ajilta akhta'ta hazzak because if you're hasty

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:54.220
you'll make a mistake.

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:56.740
You'll make a mistake.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:02.140
Wa kun sahlan layyinan lil-qaribi wal-ba'id and be easygoing and gentle

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:05.660
with people who are close to you and people who are not close to you.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:09.820
Wa la takun jabbaran 'anida and do not be

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:10.900
a

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:13.480
tyrannical person.

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:18.799
Someone who is stubborn and obstinate and difficult to be with and who is harsh with

00:04:18.799 --> 00:04:19.439
others.
